Reason:
`phys_addr_t` is defined as a 64-bit type on architectures that support physical addresses beyond 32 bits (e.g., ARM LPAE). Changing the variable types to `phys_addr_t` ensures the full physical address is preserved, preventing truncation and enabling correct command encoding.

